diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111356.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111356.patch","merged_at":"2025-10-13T17:37:06Z"},"body":"Fixes #100138.\r\n\r\nThe specialization constant patching code was rejecting signed values, assuming it needed to set the MSB to respect LLVM IR's VBR encoding. However, as explained [here](https://llvm.org/docs/BitCodeFormat.html#variable-width-integer), the contents of the integer actually do not matter at all, because we can just keep emitting continue bits even if the bits are all zero.\r\n\r\nGodot already uses an appropriate sentinel value to enforce 32 bits in the output bytecode, so this approach works fine.","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111356/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":1,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111356/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}